mark.","Loadings rise in a crisis, so a model fitted in calmer times tends to understate losses; the bias column shows by how much.","No reference portfolio holds any of the funds the factors are built from, so none of them predicts itself.","The reference portfolios are funds that still exist. A fund that closed is not in the sample, which flatters broad-market results slightly.","A portfolio you hold today has no observed history as a portfolio. Replaying it through the past is a reconstruction and is reported separately, in the Crisis replay."],"content_sha256":"1d44c9f68f75f470d72129775043d10cff43a585cf6001714255ec619cfa8039","hash_verified":true,"model_version_current":true}